What is WebAssembly?

WebAssembly (WASM) is a low-level binary instruction format that allows programs written in languages like C, C++, Rust, Go, C#, etc., to run inside web browsers at near-native speed.

Simply,

WebAssembly is a technology that allows high-performance applications to run on the web.

It works alongside JavaScript.

Simple Definition

Before WebAssembly:

Browser → JavaScript → Execute

After WebAssembly:

Browser
   ├── JavaScript
   └── WebAssembly

Both run inside the browser.